  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "slzunehgF8ZOK8UWjjMdePKXCJI=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:32.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## No monolithic schema\n\nSwitchboard does not expose one hand-maintained schema. Every Reactor Package ships its **own** GraphQL schema fragment \u2014 its subgraph \u2014 and Switchboard composes all of them into a single unified endpoint at `/graphql`.\n\nThe practical payoff is cross-package querying. A client can pull data owned by two completely independent packages in one request, and neither package needs to know the other exists:\n\n```graphql\nquery {\n  todoList(id: \"doc-123\") {\n    id\n    todos {\n      id\n      title\n      done\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThat query hits one endpoint. Behind it, whichever package owns the `todoList` type resolves it.\n\n## Each subgraph exposes three things\n\n- **Queries** \u2014 for reading documents and processor read models.\n- **Mutations** \u2014 for dispatching actions to documents.\n- **Custom types** \u2014 the domain-specific GraphQL types your resolvers return.\n\n## Why this makes the package the unit of delivery\n\nBecause a package owns its subgraph, shipping the package ships its API. There is no central schema registry to update, no coordination step, no separate gateway config to edit. Installing a package into a Switchboard extends the supergraph.\n\nComposition is also not a one-shot boot step. `GraphQLManager` keeps subgraphs in a map keyed by supergraph name, registers each one, and rebuilds the router; document-model subgraphs are *regenerated* when models are loaded dynamically, so packages installed after startup still land in the composed schema. Duplicate subgraph names are skipped rather than merged \u2014 a name collision silently loses the second registration.\n\nOne endpoint is not quite everything: the per-drive subgraph is served separately at `/d/:driveId` and is deliberately excluded from the `/graphql` supergraph.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/02-Learn/06-switchboard/02-subgraphs.mdx, packages/reactor-api/src/graphql/graphql-manager.ts (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:32.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:32.000Z"
    }
  },
